      "notes": [
         {
            "category": "description",
            "text": "Maypole versions from 2.10 through 2.13 for Perl generates session ids insecurely. The session id is seeded with the system time (which is available from HTTP response headers), a call to the built-in rand() function, and the PID.",
            "title": "Vulnerability Description"
         }
